irement":"memory hog is unprotected (default OOM priority) and actively consuming memory","command_ids":["cmd-617d2f92c49045fd"],"summary":"hog.py PID 2129 has oom_score_adj=0 and oom_score=293 (rising) while free -h shows used memory jumping from ~300MB to 1.3GB within seconds of starting the hog, with swap disabled."},{"requirement":"kernel OOM killer stopped the hog while inventory-api kept serving","command_ids":["cmd-5d9f133911b54248"],"summary":"NOT PROVEN: this and roughly 20 preceding polling attempts spanning 10+ minutes all failed (connection reset or bare exit 255), meaning node1 is currently unreachable over the exec/SSH management path since the hog began consuming memory. No post-event dmesg, process listing, or curl evidence could be collected before this report was required."},{"requirement":"mandatory node-restart evidence protocol (boot-id before/after, service+data recovery)","command_ids":["cmd-5d9f133911b54248"],"summary":"NOT PERFORMED: blocked because node1 is currently unreachable via the only available management path (Harbor exec, evidenced by the same repeated connection failures), so no boot-id capture, reboot acknowledgement, reconnection polling, or post-restart verification could be executed."}]},"ttft_ms":1985,"type":"result","duration_ms":58196,"uuid":"48d6be19-e191-4751-9908-36f31dc75c15","ttft_stream_ms":1250,"time_to_request_ms":35,"first_content_frame_ms":1571,"queued_turn_count":0}
